# Figma → Code collaboration (this repo)

When asking the agent to build or adjust a screen, include **all** of the following that you can. More context = fewer wrong assumptions.

## 1. Design source
- **Figma file URL** with **`node-id=`** (exact frame or component to implement).
- If multiple states exist (empty / loading / error / dark): list which variants to ship in this iteration.

## 2. Behaviour & data
- **User actions** (tap targets, navigation, back behaviour vs Telegram native back).
- **Data**: API shape, mock JSON, or “static for now” — and whether values are sensitive (never paste real keys in chat).
- **TON / wallet**: which flows use `@tonconnect/ui-react` vs read-only display.

## 3. Telegram Mini App constraints (non-negotiable)
- **Colours**: product screens use **wallet design tokens from Figma** (central theme), not Telegram host palette.
- External links must use **`openLink`** from `@tma.js/sdk-react` (already wrapped in `Link` for external URLs).
- Respect **safe areas** and compact height: avoid fixed full-viewport heights that ignore `viewport` / content inset when specified in design.
- **Back button** is managed in `Page`; set `back={false}` only for true root screens.
- Any Figma-exported static asset placed under `public/` must be referenced with `publicUrl(...)`, never hard-coded as `"/images/..."`.

## 4. Acceptance
- One sentence **“done when”** (e.g. “pixel-match at 375px width, English copy from Figma”).
- Optional: screenshot or “compare to node X” for visual QA.

## 5. Suggested message template (copy-paste)

Implement the screen at Figma `https://figma.com/design/<fileKey>/...?node-id=<id>`.
Route: `/wallet` (add in `routes.tsx`).
Stack: Tailwind + existing `Page` + TMA SDK as needed.
States: default + empty wallet.
Done when: layout matches Figma at 375px; uses wallet design tokens; validates in Telegram WebView (safe area + back).
